{{Term/Store|Critical Hit|Critical Hits|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are a recurring mechanic in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Tips">{{Cite|{{Big|Critical Hits}}<br/>Hitting a monster or enemy in the head with an arrow deals double the normal amount of damage.|Tips and Tricks|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Critical Hits}}<br/>Hitting a monster or enemy in the head with an arrow deals double the normal amount of damage.|Tips and Tricks|TotK}}</ref>

==Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Critical Hits are strikes that deal twice the normal damage for a [[Weapon]]. There are three ways to achieve this effect: hitting an [[Enemy]]'s head or [[Eye]] with an [[Arrow]],<ref>{{Cite|Hit an enemy's head with an arrow to perform a {{Color BotW|Red|Critical Hit}} that deals 2x damage.|N/A|BotW}}</ref><ref name="BotW Tips"/> successfully throwing a Weapon at an Enemy,<ref>{{Cite|Throw a weapon at an enemy to perform a {{Color BotW|Red|Critical Hit}}, dealing twice the weapon damage.|N/A|BotW}}</ref> and breaking a Weapon while striking an Enemy.<ref>{{Cite|Any attack that causes your weapon to break becomes a {{Color BotW|Red|Critical Hit}}, dealing 2x damage.|N/A|BotW}}</ref> Weapons can be found with a Critical Hit [[Weapon Bonus]], which increases the likelihood of landing a Critical Hit in the final blow of a chain of attacks. A unique sound effect will play to indicate a Critical Hit: a high-pitch sound when an Arrow is shot, and a loud popping sound for melee Weapons.

[[Sneakstrike]]s are a similar phenomenon, which deal more damage by stealthily attacking an unaware enemy from behind.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}
Critical Hits return in {{TotK}}, and they are attainable by the same methods present in {{BotW}}. In addition, another way to perform a Critical Strike is to attack [[Enemy|Enemies]] with a [[One-Handed Weapon]] while riding a [[Horse]] at full speed.

If Link shoots an Arrow at the head of an Enemy in a [[Monster Encampment]], such as a [[Bokoblin]] standing on a raised platform, they will receive 10 times the damage as opposed to twice as much.<ref>{{Cite Web|quote= |author= KnightPohtaytoe |title= Did you know this about Headshots in Tears of the Kingdom? |url= https://www.youtube.com/shorts/0tHq8nrceOs |archive= |published= June 14, 2025 |retrieved= June 14, 2025 |site= |type= }}</ref>

